IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-schedule1`

-- je21-tests-schedule1: tests for Schedule 1 and Article 15(6) and (7).
-- The expected values were written by hand from Schedule 1 and Article 15 before the module was run.
-- Schedule 1 lists seventeen powers, (a) to (q), and each is a power of the Board; the seventeen lines below are one for each paragraph, in the Schedule's order.

§ `Schedule 1 -- tests`

§§ `Every paragraph of Schedule 1 is a power`

#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(a): to amend the citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(b): to consolidate or split legislation, or relocate a provision into different legislation`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(c): to rearrange the provisions of legislation, or a list in a provision`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(d): to add a table of contents or destinations`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(e): to add a heading to a provision that has none, or alter a heading`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(f): to omit any map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(g): to change a reference to reflect a change of name, transfer of function or provision for construction`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(h): to make adaptations and amendments that appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(i): to change words to make them gender neutral`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(j): to change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(l): to alter words to secure uniformity of expression`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(m): to shorten a phrase or sentence`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(n): to change the wording for the better application of plain language principles`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(o): to add numbering to, or renumber, a provision`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(p): to substitute a reference to legislation that has been re-enacted or replaced`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(q): to do all other things that appear to the Board to be necessary to render revised legislation consistent with current drafting practice`)

§§ `Article 14 changes and a change with no power named`

#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Article 14` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors`)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (`a power in Article 14` `the removal of a provision relating to its commencement`)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` `no power is stated`

§§ `Article 15(6) and (7): lists of changes`

`a change under Schedule 1(i)` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "words made gender neutral", `a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(i): to change words to make them gender neutral`
`a change under Schedule 1(h)` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "an adaptation after a constitutional change", `a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(h): to make adaptations and amendments that appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes`
`a change under Article 14` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "a typographical error corrected", `a power in Article 14` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors`
`a change with no power named` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "a change nobody has authority for", `no power is stated`

#ASSERT `Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change under Article 14`)
#ASSERT `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change under Article 14`)
#ASSERT `Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(h)`)
#ASSERT `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(h)`)
-- One change with no power named spoils the list, wherever it stands in it.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change with no power named`)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change with no power named`)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` (LIST `a change with no power named`, `a change under Article 14`)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` (LIST `a change with no power named`, `a change under Article 14`)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` (LIST `a change with no power named`)
-- No change at all: vacuously within.
#ASSERT `Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` (EMPTY)

§§ `Article 15(7): certification`

#ASSERT `Article 15(7): certification is open to the Board` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 15(7): certification is open to the Board` FALSE
